-1 \cdot (y + 1) \\
1 \cdot (x - 1)
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
- y - 1 \\
x - 1
\end{bmatrix}
$$

3. Translate back by adding $ (1, -1) $:

$$
(x', y') = \left( - y - 1 + 1, x - 1 - 1 \right) = (- y, x - 2)
$$

